{
  "work_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis",
  "source_path": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis.json",
  "source_language": "chu",
  "target_language": "eng",
  "provenance": {
    "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29": {
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "prompt_version": "bulk-2026-10-12",
      "date": "2026-10-29",
      "script": "__main__"
    }
  },
  "translations": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "8f012c28a2464659",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And many believed in him. When the governor heard this, he ordered him to be brought in. When Alexander arrived, the governor said to him:"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "8aedb6c1bd244b9f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "“Tell me, who are you, deceiving so many and turning them away from sacrifices to the gods,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "c8295a32098a9b96",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and teaching them another faith? Tell us, then, who you are to deceive the people like this.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "f3f9a56669f9325f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “I am a Christian, and my rank is that of a priest."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "9c471d22d0768c9e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "In this office, governor, I have hoped through faith to receive what is hoped for in Christ.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "8e6e7ce26071d199",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Antoninus said, “And who is Christ?” Alexander said, “The Savior of the whole world,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "eae4b53cf5e99cc4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and the light of those who believe in him.” Antoninus said, “How can he be a savior when he was crucified"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "6128a7ce7dba7ac2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and suffered death?” Alexander said, “This is the wonder, governor: that he died in the flesh,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "dafdad31ccce62da",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "so that he might not only enlighten [?], but also free the dead from suffering in Hades.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "d6a1be3a631f81d7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Antoninus said, “You speak foolish words and much nonsense. How, then, can someone who could not help himself help others?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "9bbe978e1e7a800b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “His death gives those who believe in him life"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "6f1edd372a0c1447",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and imperishability in heaven.” Antoninus said, “Then stop speaking nonsense and sacrifice to the gods.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79r.s13",
      "source_sha256": "996a5480b5624550",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “I am not speaking nonsense when I say this. But if I obey you,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "e29981744d55e750",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "then I am not only deluded but a fool, for your words are foolish.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "daa1cd1a9b24412b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Antoninus said, “By the gods, if you obey and sacrifice to the gods, you will be the master of great wealth."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "4b80b8dba2db0aca",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But if you do not obey, I will destroy you with cruel tortures.” Alexander said, “Do not deceive yourself, governor,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "646b0e8aa868228b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "that I will listen to your flattery and miss Christ’s coming. For he is the living God.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "9749f3b3d036e4a1",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Antoninus said, “If you do not sacrifice, I will display you before everyone under torture.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "af7ce983c2c2456a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “I will die in cruel torments at Christ’s hands if I obey you and sacrifice to unclean demons.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "30b1b2ee7ad14a60",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Antoninus said, “Strip him and beat him on the belly with raw sinews.” While he was being beaten and saying nothing,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "c11008f1e41c54f3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "the governor said to him, “Obey me, Alexander, and sacrifice to the gods.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "f155a077f1428bcc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “Your tortures are nothing, you tormentor,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "dfa68875f8884478",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and I will not sacrifice. I have already told you that I am a Christian and that there is a God in heaven"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "9a368bc70704a315",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who helps me.” Antoninus said, “Did I not tell you to abandon this nonsense and come forward and sacrifice,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "ccc10257e3d84012",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "so that the emperor’s will may be done?” Alexander said, “I offer sacrifice to the eternal King.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.79v.s13",
      "source_sha256": "75f7f149b29dd8b7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who made heaven and earth, and the sea and everything"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "8dbbeab7cd6b9ef0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "in them. Antoninus said, “Do they not seem to you to be gods, those to whom the sovereign emperor himself offers sacrifices?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "c2f0f886efa13b5a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “Great amazement seizes me, governor. May we someday see even you yourself repenting of the deception of idols"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "8375f48bae05b6c1",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and turning to the truth.” Antoninus said, “Are you mad, Alexander?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "ff56b0d21b9f5b28",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “I am not mad, but I fear God and his Son Jesus Christ,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "a72ad5248eb25cc8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who has power over soul and body on the day of judgment.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "0c847093a967b202",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Antoninus said, “Kindle a fire and heat the pan, so that he may be thrown into it"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "721389987ccb2363",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and his sorcery may thereby be overcome.” When the fire had been kindled, they heated the pan"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "d393a206371dbb66",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "until it was like fire. Antoninus said to him, “Alexander, offer sacrifice,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "42b55cf129b6385d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "so that you do not end up in the pan. Christ, whom you worship, will be of no help to you.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "3618239cabfb4979",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “You are not saying this of your own accord, but at the prompting of your father Satan,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "0b9df21431c68ad0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "through whose dignity you have been filled with wisdom.” Antoninus said, “Let him be thrown into the pan,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "1dc2213d84608321",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "so that I may see what help the one who was crucified and died will give him.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80r.s13",
      "source_sha256": "82866a9c10328cf7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander joyfully leaped into the pan. He went in alone, but he could be seen in the pan"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "1d73cac22900a5d1",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "as one of three. When he had entered the pan, dew came from heaven, and the pan became as though it had never known fire."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "d481eace03badbdb",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander was praising God and saying, “God, who reigns forever and sits upon the cherubim,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "2de5d582f5254b7b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "whom the angels and archangels praise, I, the sinner,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "f5c06f0415ffab4c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander, bless you, because you worked wonders for your servant Daniel, shut the lion’s mouth,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "33af1e2a3131f470",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "crushed all the power of his adversaries, and crowned your servant. Now also hear me, God,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "af23180aeffc9852",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and show this Antoninus, who is unworthy of your blessings,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "ed02c21e91b2bac3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "that his hopes are intertwined with demons, who, being imperfect themselves,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "51f991258ddaa29b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "make those who hope in them imperfect.” Antoninus said, “I told you, Alexander, that you have a demon,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "ead3631cc593a932",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and trusting in it, you feel no shame.” Alexander said, “Do you not understand, foolish man,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "f5bbd1ee202bfcf6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "that a demon is never tormented with such torments, but requires sacrifices and the fumes of useless sacrifices,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "11fd407ed50af53d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "which plunge people into destruction?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "2fdf669d8cf78b3f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Having learned from him, you have become a teacher yourself and entered into a fiery kinship."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.80v.s13",
      "source_sha256": "dfb6b2df43c04504",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And you make those tortured with you your companions.” Antoninus said, “Set four wooden posts in the ground, stretch him out along the posts, and bind"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "71902344124f1091",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "him tightly, so that, stretched out by the posts, he will be broken and offer sacrifice, or else, exposed, die a miserable death.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "7c0391a95fe48e5d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said as he was being tortured, “Your devices are nothing.” And Alexander was brought forward and stretched out on the posts."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "0c1efe45968df220",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The valiant martyr of Christ endured such torture, seeing all his limbs stretched out"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "a588c9b2d0020308",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and all his bones being broken. Speaking with great wisdom, Alexander said, “You are the God of the Christians,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "ec0b74bf04421c89",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who have come to the saints who pleased you. Come also to me, a sinner, and show that your name is great"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "44804a152f3cfbee",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and [?] those who fear you.” When he had said this, his face changed"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "d957968d39c93a8f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and became like a flame. One of those serving before the governor approached him"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "6e3d5b5cc06da347",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and said to him, “It is clear to everyone, Alexander, that you are prevailing through sorcery."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "fa1cea060e4f0c0b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For your face looked pale, but now it is bright as the sun.” Alexander said, “You rightly said it was pale,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "57263b924676c127",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "because of bodily weakness. For everyone suffering bodily pain grows very pale. But the brightness you now see"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "e4ce41bf0ee011d4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "is because of endurance and God’s providence. For everyone who endures is saved forever.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "e8affa740d109524",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The servant said, “Then is it because of endurance that your face changes?” Alexander said, “Yes."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "5600088780b31cc6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Learn this yourself, then, O man: every Christian who seeks hope in God will readily find it."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "d6e899662f19c1f2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For earthly wealth is obtained with toil and great suffering, and through it souls that lack self-restraint go to destruction."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "53da84f0953137b6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And many here are now seeking it. But wealth toward God comes quickly and brings thankfulness;"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "8ea877243ab6e751",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "it is easily obtained: the kingdom of heaven can be acquired not with gold or silver, but with lowly copper.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "ed2ffb6a2ecbd1ee",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Hearing this, the servant said, “Guide me, I beg you, so that perhaps I too may be able to share in it forever and ever.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "fdd7de9c66cacd8d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “Believe in God and in Christ, through whom you will have life forever and ever.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "6b4e6fd5e8583773",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The servant said, “O God, who help your servant Alexander, help me also, a sinner."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "d900802b9c88c54e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Draw me away from foul defilement, from the falsely named gods, and from their deception,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "84993f5580fbed86",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and from the wrath of the ungodly Antoninus, the author of every evil."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "c1c02dc3a9297a61",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And count me among your servants together with your servant Alexander.” And Alexander said, “O God, may your will be done"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "02a09185df3e1259",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "in answer to your servant’s prayer.” The governor heard his prayers."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.81v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "fc134ea2ca7f85d5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "As he cried out to God, he became angry and killed him, saying, “A fellow participant"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "d32ba2aaa04dca00",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "in Alexander’s impending death you shall be, and end your life confessing your faith in martyrdom.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "8f6e08464a4c48e6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He also ordered the brave Alexander to be hung up and scraped. While he was being scraped, he cried out, saying, “I am a Christian.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "341849fc6614f34f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He ordered them to tear him still more. While he was being scraped, he formed the sign of the cross in his mind."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "b378e37cf1b22e52",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Raising his eyes to heaven, he said, “Blessed are you, Lord God of our fathers,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "2c027f433372eeef",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who, through the most valiant struggles, have made your servant Alexander steadfast in knowing you."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "adee4815ec78d7d1",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "See how you have brought the torture inflicted by the vile Antoninus to shame.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "5368622d49e16ae6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Hearing this, the governor ordered them to tear him again and pour vinegar mixed with salt over him,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "dc64ab547efaf241",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and to rub his wounds with cloth, to see whether he could force him by these tortures to offer sacrifice."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "3e0360377680739c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But he again said in a loud voice, “Are you not ashamed, O torturer, of the evils you have committed"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "4315474a38181cfe",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and of pleasing demons? For if there were no human craftsmanship, you would have no god."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "be1c3dfd319175ac",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But you, lacking understanding and bearing their likeness, are blind; you cling to the blind and have blind hopes."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "3d747863518bf922",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For what you saw a short time ago being forged with hammers and shaped with an axe, you have now set"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "728c3ca750e3252a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "up and call it a god. Therefore I will not obey you, nor will your terrors or your tortures frighten me."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "df60b144d6074eb5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For I have God, the King of all ages, protecting me.” As he was saying this, the wounds from his flaying ran together,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "d5cd2f5fead0aa3b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "so that all his flesh was laid bare. All those standing there were astonished and said, “How does this man endure it?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "c07159d33ebe5b7f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When holy Alexander would not heed the governor’s persuasion, nor his coercion, nor his blows,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "3cb87f6f3baf8030",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "nor his anger, the governor, the princeps, said, “Alexander, abandon your folly, obey, and sacrifice to the gods,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "1a258475a9e37688",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and you will be the emperor’s friend.” He answered him, for his heart was turned toward God."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "aaf46682bed6b355",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The sound of a voice was heard [?] on the right and on the left, saying:"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "bc97cec9bbbb6924",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "“Take courage and be strong, Alexander, for my name’s sake."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "e88cdf78215bd187",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For I will deliver you from every torture and from the governor’s hands.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "0d375438b6b9d382",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When the voice was heard, everyone was astonished and said, “Where does this voice come from?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "34614d8da27d61f9",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Dalmatius the princeps became frightened and prodded Alexander, saying, “What is this voice"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "bf312d7eeed129b9",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "that has come to you?” Then Alexander again made the sign of the cross by the grace of God."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.82v.s13",
      "source_sha256": "5c120ac72c4286cd",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Beginning at his forehead, he made the sign of the cross over his whole body, saying, “Lord,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "1b2488520484b8c4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Almighty, blessed are you,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "d44bc873de71d3da",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and may your name be glorified, you who this present day, for your servant’s everlasting joy,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "adc61070d89c5dec",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "have bestowed as a gift. And fill your servant’s soul with your goodness,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "bbf88861c4b8c713",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and show the lawless and godless Antoninus and Dalmatius"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "b646e59ceb0f9944",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "that you are the God of the Christians and that you reward those who put their trust in you.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "0894c33880ff71d8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then Antoninus said again, “Alexander, sacrifice to the gods.” Alexander said, “I told you that I will not sacrifice to your gods,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "3e9c3f9124f7a9ac",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "which are worthless, deaf, and blind.” Antoninus said, “How long will you blaspheme and refuse to do the emperor’s will?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "dc0c4bd8424a5a1d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Keep yourself safe and sound from every wound. You are of noble birth; do not bring yourself low.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "c213cd5cbe988533",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “I marvel at how foolishly you behave in calling them gods."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "73166c8d30befade",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "How can these be gods, when they neither see nor feel nor smell?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "5459dcdf3e4e950c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Yet you cling to them, having abandoned the living and true God and his only-begotten Son, Jesus Christ,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "41594fa939015050",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who exists and existed before the ages, and you put your trust in pagan temples and unclean demons."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83r.s13",
      "source_sha256": "9894bf533f3fe47d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "So do whatever you wish, for I have told you that I am a Christian,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "5f920a5719e5e9f0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and your tortures do not touch me.” Antoninus said to his servants, “Light a fire, take him down from the wooden frame,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "c99d294a96ed7d2c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and throw him into the fire, so that the fire may destroy him.” When the fire had been lit,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "145f89943a036327",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander was led forward, guided by two angels, who went into the fire with him"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "5f0818505e883707",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and scattered the flames. Standing in the middle of the furnace, Alexander said, “Holy are you, O God,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "75e4cc1c3b050033",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who in your divinity have sent down to poor Alexander"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "bfbab8b622690fad",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "help from heaven, to show that all things are subject to you. Even the blazing tongues of flame,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "ce5f2d2370728b95",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "which could not withstand the entrance of your warriors or your fearful and awe-inspiring command,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "e47abb4429a36237",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "have died down around me, but they scorch the mind of the lawless and impious man.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "8096f2e7f28a3d36",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The governor became enraged and ordered him to be brought out. He said to him, “Sacrifice to the gods, so that I may spare you"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "37546738f41de8c0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and send you to the emperor with great honor.” Alexander said, “You command me to sacrifice and abandon the truth,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "8ad48553baeb0c6d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "so that I may become the friend of a man subject to the same weaknesses as I am.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.83v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "408ca2bd415e15b6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and I shall become an enemy of God who made me, and instead of incorruptible things, corruption"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "f31a289a5e8f040a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "I shall gain. But rather let me disregard a man subject to the same passions as I am,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "a065393e60f40c55",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who is alive today and dies tomorrow, and fear him who exists forever"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "b8d77bdc6a3645fc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and existed before all things, who has prepared for the faithful things that no eye has seen and no ears have heard."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "e956fe749fa17fc3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Antoninus said, “Well! You have not only scorned the gods, but have also reviled the emperors."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "e7f44c1a7d53d618",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Therefore I shall have the beasts tear out your lungs while you are still alive.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "2d5def47b97fac3e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “Once, twice, and many times I have told you that for Christ’s sake I do not fear your tortures."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "1f2520d8997b31d1",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For they do not touch me. For if I had not known what is said: ‘You shall not put the Lord your God to the test.’"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "c0592ff3f111a099",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Having pledged myself to God, how can I return to the foolish and useless faith of demons,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "472943b10f68ea5c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "when the Lord has said that those who believe in them shall be like them, deaf and motionless?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "1d0c1220b2ebfe8d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But I tell you again: devise, O tormentor, the greatest tortures you have,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "a69876dd9dea0c2d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "so that at least in this way you may learn that they are powerless, not only against me alone, but against all"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "4f37536b2975d9a2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who endure hardship for his name’s sake.” Antoninus said, “Now I know that you sustain yourself by sorcery and much demonic possession. Those words expose you:"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "babf09dc42b9eb7d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "you are not suffering for the sake of Christ, of whom you speak, but you practice sorcery and deceive everyone.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "deb0dc39e872ed39",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Alexander said, “May it be your lot, you defiler, filled with such deeds, to rule"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "72b641681077b239",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "with your father the devil. For to me, to live is Christ, and to die is gain.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "2c1d281f0214e486",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Antoninus said, “Let him be taken to the arena, to the beasts.” And as soon as he entered, with the governor seated,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "be4956c81fae710c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "he made the sign of the cross, raised his eyes to heaven, and said in a loud voice, “Quickly carry out, you ungodly man,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "d97967cc611bfe3a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "you most impious of all, Antoninus the tormentor, the will of your father Satan."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "dacf1b74c9ecd4d5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For I am ready, protected by the sign of Christ, to scorn your short-lived tortures.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "4087a7b53d4169c5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When he had said this, they opened the beasts’ enclosure, and a lion came out roaring."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "df16d8b018214806",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And just as a loving father welcomes his child, so the lion ran up and leaped upon the righteous man,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "cc74c7a53f2bbffc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "placed its paws beneath his arms, licked the righteous man’s sweat, and gazed at him,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "b9b02a2de2e5a83a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "asking for God’s direction, so that the people might perhaps understand. As the lion groaned in this way, the keeper of the beasts opened the enclosure again,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/vita-alexandri-sidensis#Supr.84v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "57267d2b67bec5fd",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and another lion came out and fell at the saint’s feet, gazing into his face. And there came out"
    }
  ]
}
